                        "glosses": [
                            "通灵术"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "27417b3d-4ea0-4dc7-8893-d7b1b7fdbed2",
                                "sense_id": "e8b5c1c0-7cd8-31f9-9638-b33cb7ea1cf4",
                                "text": "And for to make this treatise the more pleasaunt and facill, I have put it in forme of a Dialogue, which I have diuided into three bookes: The first speaking of Magie in general, and Necromancie in special."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d777a0a3-bfa1-444d-afec-de457e3211f8",
                                "sense_id": "e8b5c1c0-7cd8-31f9-9638-b33cb7ea1cf4",
                                "text": "And in one word for all, Nagomancy, or Necromancy; by inspecting, consulting, and divining by, with，或源自the dead."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f69f593-c29a-4e81-ad3f-4ad0bbfc021a",
                                "sense_id": "e8b5c1c0-7cd8-31f9-9638-b33cb7ea1cf4",
                                "text": "the Devil did often tempt me to study necromancy and nigromancy and to make use of magic, and to make a league with him..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d651ad0d-9275-4b22-a075-52d821a69110",
                                "sense_id": "e8b5c1c0-7cd8-31f9-9638-b33cb7ea1cf4",
                                "text": "There is no doubt..that necromancy is the touch-stone of occultism..."
                            }
                        ]
